// © @Apeaverage & @SXDXST_FB6 (Impulse MACD) • Refined by Akash (SMA/RSI/MACD)
//
// ═══ iAPE v4 — THE one script (engine v2.2, validated; formerly SWING_PRO v3) ═══════════
// Consolidates and SUPERSEDES every earlier SWING_PRO / Swing1m script (see legacy/).  iAPE v4 = product rebrand of SWING_PRO v3 — NO engine changes; all validation evidence carries over.
// One script = the strategy (backtestable P&L), the on-chart BUY/SELL/EXIT signals,
// the alerts, and a plain-English dashboard — all driven by the same logic.
//
// v2 CHANGES (evidence: backtest/reports/ablation_2026-07-01.md):
//   • REMOVED price-vs-trend entry gate (provably dead — zero trades changed).
//   • REMOVED 1.5× volume gate (halved trades, WORSENED per-trade expectancy).
//   • MACD-flip exit OFF by default (it cut winners before target; PF 0.93 → 1.00).
//   • REMOVED reversal entries + anti-chase (dead code in every tested config).
//   • Default direction LONGS ONLY (shorts bled in every configuration tested).
//
// v2.1 CHANGES (evidence: walk-forward + MTF + orthogonal tests, 2y Alpaca SIP data):
//   • HONESTY HEADER: entry selection has ~zero out-of-sample edge on its own; the
//     spring-2026 brilliance was REGIME. Treat signals as a disciplined framework —
//     not a money printer. Paper-trade first. Size small.
//   • EXECUTION carries value: "5m decisions, 1m fills" was the best tested config
//     (PF 1.10). TV Premium: set use_bar_magnifier=true below.
//   • 1m-trigger entries REJECTED (PF 0.82, 0/5 symbols). Regime gates REJECTED
//     (sign-flip out of sample). Daily flow data (DIX/GEX/FINRA): ~1σ, not coded in.
//   • Plain-English dashboard + live stop/target lines.
//
// v2.2 CHANGES (evidence: exit_sweep_2026-07-02.md — 64 exit configs, H2-VALIDATED):
//   • Pure stop + 3R target: +$6,835 / PF 1.30 over 2y vs +$1,706 / 1.08 for the old
//     exits, consistent in BOTH data halves. Every "protective" exit (partial, BE,
//     trend-cross, MACD-flip) was clipping the rare big winners that carry the system.
//   • NEW MODE SELECTOR (group 1): Validated / Strict / Comfort — same 7 indicators
//     in every mode, only thresholds & exits change. Strict is UNVALIDATED and being
//     shadow-scored against live prices in the forward test; Comfort's cost is
//     measured and printed in its tooltip. Win rate is a dial, not an edge.
//
// v2.2.1 RESEARCH NOTES (through 2026-07-03):
//   • PARITY CONFIRMED: the Python research engine matches this script trade-for-trade
//     (largest TSLA win within $1) — every number in these comments was measured on
//     logic verified identical to this chart.
//   • MORE REJECTIONS (tested, buried — don't resurrect): extension veto (the
//     "chasing" entries ARE the profitable ones), pullback-only entries, loss
//     cooldowns, 1-hour port (all its shine was year-one), limit entries & time-stops
//     (a wash: 97% fill rate means the savings equal the missed winners).
//   • SIZING STUDY (18 rules): flat 10%-of-equity beat equal-risk sizing, position
//     caps and daily loss-stops on return-per-unit-of-drawdown. Left unchanged.
//   • MONTE CARLO (10,000 shuffles of 857 trades): for a WORKING system, losing
//     streaks up to 12 and a losing 6-week stretch are NORMAL — 17.5% of 6-week
//     windows lose money even when nothing is broken. The dashboard now tracks your
//     live losing streak against that threshold. Read it before doubting the system.
//   • LIVE EXPERIMENTS: two baskets paper-trading head-to-head (AAPL NVDA TSLA MSFT
//     META vs MSTR ORCL NFLX AVGO CRWD); STRICT mode shadow-scored on live prices.
//     Consistent in BOTH data halves (bench for basket v3): AVGO CRWD ARM MU WMT
//     PLTR KLAC INTC.
//
// v3 HEADLINE (evidence: daily_30y_2026-07-04.md) — THE FLAGSHIP FINDING:
//   The seven-gate engine was a DAILY system aimed at the wrong clock all along.
//   On DAILY bars across THREE market generations (1995-2026, 22 long-history names
//   incl. era-losers GE/IBM/INTC): PF 1.47 / 2.03 / 2.45 by decade, 1,090 trades,
//   +0.43R avg, ALL 22 SYMBOLS PROFITABLE — survived the dot-com bust, 2008, COVID,
//   the 2022 bear. On 5m it merely broke even (noise + costs); at daily, trend
//   persistence is real and costs are a rounding error. → OPEN THIS ON A DAILY CHART.
//   The script auto-switches to the validated daily config there (local trend regime).
//   5m remains a running paper experiment; 1m is REJECTED; 1h FAILED. The dashboard's
//   "This timeframe" row tells you which chart you're standing on is proven.
//   Companion mean-reversion system (anti-correlated, for a 2-strategy portfolio):
//   iAPE_MR.pine. Same house rule — paper-audition before real money.
//
// Set your broker's real commission + slippage in Properties. Not financial advice.
//@version=6
// $2K SMALL-BOOK CONFIG (2026-07-14): initial_capital=2000 + 22% sizing to match the live
// Webull paper book. NOT a validated improvement — the sizing study validated flat 10% on a
// $100k book; 22% is the small-book accommodation (whole-share floor: $200/trade buys ZERO
// shares of most large caps → zero trades → empty report). At $440/trade, symbols over ~$440
// (COST, CAT, GS, DE...) still size to 0 shares and will show no trades — test on affordable
// names (KO, XOM, WMT, DIS, CVX, BA, AAPL, JPM, HD, UNH). Expect ~4 concurrent positions max.
strategy("iAPE v4 — Momentum (daily flagship)", shorttitle="iAPE_v4", overlay=true,
     max_labels_count=500, pyramiding=0, calc_on_every_tick=false,
     initial_capital=2000, default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=22,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.01, slippage=1,
     use_bar_magnifier=false)  // <- TV Premium? set true = the validated "1m fills" upgrade

// ── 1) Direction, mode & signal basics ────────────────────────────────────────────────
g1 = "1) Direction & signals"
tradeDir = input.string("Buys only (long)", "Trade direction", options=["Buys only (long)", "Both", "Sells only (short)"], group=g1, tooltip="Validated default is LONGS ONLY: across 2 years, every configuration lost money on the short side. Switch only to re-test, not to trade on faith.")
mode = input.string("Validated (v2.2)", "Mode", options=["Validated (v2.2)", "Strict - higher win%? (UNVALIDATED)", "Comfort - more winners, lower profit"], group=g1, tooltip="Same 7 indicators in every mode - only thresholds/exits change.\n\nVALIDATED: the config that won 2 years of out-of-sample testing (PF 1.30, ~37% win, 3R winners). Patience is the strategy.\n\nSTRICT: tighter gates (ADX 25+, slope 0.30+, RSI 55+) - fewer, possibly higher-quality entries. NOT yet validated; it is being shadow-scored against live prices in the forward test. Watch, don't trust.\n\nCOMFORT: v2.1 exits (partial @1R, breakeven, 2R target, trend exit). MEASURED cost: win rate rises to ~46-60% but 2-yr profit drops from $6,835 to $1,706 (PF 1.30 -> 1.08). More green checkmarks, less money - a psychology dial, not an edge.")
isStrict  = mode == "Strict - higher win%? (UNVALIDATED)"
isComfort = mode == "Comfort - more winners, lower profit"
minBarsBetween = input.int(1, "Minimum bars between trades", minval=0, group=g1)
confirmClose = input.bool(true, "Only act after the bar closes (no repainting)", group=g1)
showSignals = input.bool(true, "Show BUY / SELL / EXIT labels", group=g1)
markerSize  = input.string("Large", "Signal label size", options=["Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group=g1)
sizeOpt = markerSize == "Small" ? size.small : markerSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : markerSize == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.large
allowLongs  = tradeDir != "Sells only (short)"
allowShorts = tradeDir != "Buys only (long)"

// ── 2) Trend regime (slope filter — the workhorse) ────────────────────────────────────
g2 = "2) Trend regime — ATR-normalised slope on a bigger timeframe"
useHTFTrend  = input.bool(true,  "Judge the regime from a bigger timeframe", group=g2)
useAutoHTF   = input.bool(true,  "Pick that timeframe automatically", group=g2, tooltip="5-min chart × 15 = 75-min regime view.")
autoHtfMult  = input.int(15, "How much bigger? (× chart timeframe)", minval=2, maxval=60, step=1, group=g2)
htfTfManual  = input.timeframe("60", "Bigger timeframe (if automatic is off)", group=g2)
trendType    = input.string("EMA", "Trend line style", options=["EMA", "SMA"], group=g2)
trendLen     = input.int(50, "Trend line length (bars)", minval=10, maxval=200, step=5, group=g2)
useSlope     = input.bool(true,  "Skip flat, sideways markets (KEEP ON — validated)", group=g2, tooltip="Ablation: removing this filter turned -$144 into -$1,802 (PF 0.70). The single most protective filter in the system.")
slopeLen     = input.int(3, "Tilt lookback (HTF bars)", minval=1, group=g2)
slopeMinATR  = input.float(0.20, "How steep the trend must be", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=g2)
showTrend    = input.bool(true, "Show the trend line (also the exit line)", group=g2)

// ── 3) Momentum gates (individually marginal — kept togglable) ────────────────────────
g3 = "3) Momentum gates — each togglable for A/B testing"
useMACDGate  = input.bool(true, "Require MACD agreement", group=g3, tooltip="MACD, Impulse and RSI largely triple-vote the same information; individually each is noise-level. Kept for structure, not proven edge.")
fastLength   = input.int(12, "MACD fast", minval=1, group=g3)
slowLength   = input.int(26, "MACD slow", minval=1, group=g3)
signalLength = input.int(9,  "MACD signal", minval=1, group=g3)
useImpulse   = input.bool(true, "Require Impulse MACD agreement", group=g3)
lengthMA     = input.int(34, "Impulse smoothing length", minval=1, group=g3)
lengthSignal = input.int(9,  "Impulse signal length", minval=1, group=g3)
useRSIGate   = input.bool(true, "Require RSI pressure band", group=g3)
rsiLength    = input.int(14, "RSI lookback", minval=1, group=g3)
rsiLongLevel  = input.int(52, "Buys need RSI above", group=g3)
rsiShortLevel = input.int(48, "Sells need RSI below", group=g3)

// ── 4) Trade-quality filters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
g4 = "4) Trade-quality filters"
useADX  = input.bool(true,  "Only trade when the trend is strong (ADX)", group=g4)
adxLen  = input.int(14, "ADX lookback", minval=1, group=g4)
adxMin  = input.int(20, "Minimum ADX", minval=1, maxval=50, step=1, group=g4)
useMarketFilter = input.bool(true, "Only trade with the overall market (KEEP ON — validated)", group=g4, tooltip="Ablation: removing this cost $669 on the basket (PF 0.93 → 0.74).")
marketSym   = input.symbol("SPY", "Market index to follow", group=g4)
marketMaLen = input.int(50, "Market trend length (bars)", minval=5, maxval=200, step=5, group=g4)
useCandle   = input.bool(true, "Entry bar must match — green to buy, red to sell (KEEP ON — validated)", group=g4, tooltip="Ablation: removing this cost $512 (PF 0.78).")
useSess = input.bool(false, "Only trade during set hours", group=g4)
sess    = input.session("0930-1600", "Trading hours (exchange time)", group=g4)

// ── 5) Entries ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
g5 = "5) Entries"
useStateEntry = input.bool(true, "Entry A: Trend (everything lines up)", group=g5)
usePullback   = input.bool(true, "Entry B: Buy the dip / sell the bounce", group=g5)
pullbackEMA   = input.int(9, "Fast line for dips & bounces", minval=1, group=g5)
allowReentry  = input.bool(true, "Allow trading the same direction again", group=g5)
longWinsOnConflict = input.bool(false, "If buy & sell trigger same bar, take the buy", group=g5, tooltip="Off (recommended): skip contradictory bars entirely.")

// ── 6) Exits & risk ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
g6 = "6) Exits & risk"
exitOnTrend = input.bool(false, "Exit when price closes back across the trend line (OFF — validated)", group=g6, tooltip="Exit sweep: closing on the trend cross clipped winners before the 3R target. OFF beat ON in both data halves.")
exitOnMACD  = input.bool(false, "Exit when MACD flips against you (OFF — validated)", group=g6, tooltip="This exit was cutting winners long before the profit target (PF 0.93 with it, 1.00 without).")
exitOnRSI   = input.bool(false, "Exit when RSI crosses back through 50", group=g6)
exitOnTarget = input.bool(true, "Exit at the stop-loss / profit target", group=g6)
atrLen      = input.int(14, "Volatility lookback (bars)", minval=1, group=g6)
atrStopMult = input.float(1.5, "Stop distance (volatility units)", minval=0.1, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=g6)
rrRatio     = input.float(3.0, "Profit target vs. risk (3 — validated)", minval=0.1, maxval=6.0, step=0.1, group=g6, tooltip="Exit sweep: 3R beat 2R and 2.5R in both data halves. The edge lives in the big winners — give them room.")
useStructStop = input.bool(true, "Put the stop just past the recent swing", group=g6)
structLookback = input.int(10, "Swing lookback (bars)", minval=2, maxval=50, step=1, group=g6)
structBufATR = input.float(0.25, "Extra cushion past the swing", minval=0.0, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=g6)
usePartial   = input.bool(false, "Take partial profit at a first target (OFF — validated)", group=g6, tooltip="Banking half at 1R felt safe but taxed the big winners. OFF beat ON in both data halves.")
partialPct   = input.int(50, "How much to close at first target (%)", minval=1, maxval=99, step=5, group=g6)
partialR     = input.float(1.0, "First target distance (× risk)", minval=0.2, maxval=4.0, step=0.1, group=g6)
useBreakeven = input.bool(false, "Move stop to breakeven once in profit (OFF — validated)", group=g6, tooltip="Breakeven stops got wicked out of trades that went on to hit 3R. OFF beat ON in both data halves.")
beTriggerR   = input.float(1.0, "Breakeven trigger (× risk)", minval=0.2, maxval=4.0, step=0.1, group=g6)
showRiskLines = input.bool(true, "Draw live stop & target lines while in a trade", group=g6)
showExits    = input.bool(true,  "Show EXIT / COVER markers", group=g6)

// ── 7) External confirmation hook (OrderFlow_Proxy / future flow bridge) ───────────────
g7 = "7) External confirmation — wire another indicator's line in (optional)"
useExtLong  = input.bool(false, "Buys need the connected line active", group=g7, tooltip="Pick another indicator's plotted output below (TradingView 'indicator-on-indicator'), e.g. OFLOW_PROXY: → Buy pressure. Leave OFF until actually wired.")
srcExtLong  = input.source(close, "   ↳ bullish/confirm line", group=g7)
useExtShort = input.bool(false, "Sells need the connected line active", group=g7)
srcExtShort = input.source(close, "   ↳ bearish/confirm line", group=g7)
extLevel    = input.float(0.5, "   ↳ 'active' when above", step=0.1, group=g7)

// ── 8) Backtest window, display & dashboard ────────────────────────────────────────────
g8 = "8) Backtest window & display"
useDateFilter = input.bool(false, "Only test between two dates", group=g8)
startDate = input.time(timestamp("01 Jan 2024 00:00 +0000"), "From", group=g8)
endDate   = input.time(timestamp("01 Jan 2027 00:00 +0000"), "To", group=g8)
inWindow  = not useDateFilter or (time >= startDate and time <= endDate)
buyTag  = input.string("▲ BUY", "Buy marker text", group=g8)
sellTag = input.string("▼ SELL", "Sell marker text", group=g8)
buyMarkerCol  = input.color(#26a69a, "Buy colour", group=g8)
sellMarkerCol = input.color(#e53935, "Sell colour", group=g8)
exitMarkerCol = input.color(color.orange, "Exit / cover colour", group=g8)
showDash    = input.bool(true, "Show plain-English dashboard", group=g8)
showRegime  = input.bool(true, "Show market regime (label only — changes nothing)", group=g8, tooltip="Displays the frozen switch-policy classifier: SPY above a RISING 50-day SMA = momentum weather, otherwise mean-reversion weather. This is a READ-OUT ONLY. It does not gate, delay or alter a single entry or exit — v4's own market filter (SPY vs EMA50) is untouched and is what actually decides trades. The switch policy itself is in forward shadow (since 2026-07-13, judged at 126 sessions) and has NOT been adopted.")
dashSizeStr = input.string("Normal", "Dashboard text size", options=["Small", "Normal", "Large"], group=g8)
dashSize = dashSizeStr == "Small" ? size.small : dashSizeStr == "Large" ? size.large : size.normal

// ── Mode-effective values (Strict tightens gates; Comfort restores v2.1 exits) ─────────
slopeMinATR_e   = isStrict ? math.max(slopeMinATR, 0.30) : slopeMinATR
rsiLongLevel_e  = isStrict ? math.max(rsiLongLevel, 55) : rsiLongLevel
rsiShortLevel_e = isStrict ? math.min(rsiShortLevel, 45) : rsiShortLevel
adxMin_e        = isStrict ? math.max(adxMin, 25) : adxMin
rrRatio_e       = isComfort ? 2.0 : rrRatio
usePartial_e    = isComfort ? true : usePartial
useBreakeven_e  = isComfort ? true : useBreakeven
exitOnTrend_e   = isComfort ? true : exitOnTrend

// ── Functions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
calc_smma(src, len) =>
    var float smma = na
    smma := na(smma[1]) ? ta.sma(src, len) : (smma[1] * (len - 1) + src) / len
    smma
calc_zlema(src, length) =>
    ema1 = ta.ema(src, length)
    ema2 = ta.ema(ema1, length)
    ema1 + (ema1 - ema2)

atr = ta.atr(atrLen)

// ── Trend regime: HTF MA + ATR-normalised slope (non-repainting via prior HTF bar) ─────
chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
autoSec  = chartSec * autoHtfMult
htfAuto  = autoSec % 60 == 0 ? str.tostring(int(autoSec / 60)) : str.tostring(int(autoSec)) + "S"
// iAPE-D (formerly SWING_PRO-D): on daily+ charts the validated config is the LOCAL daily trend
// (EMA50 + ATR slope on the chart itself) — the intraday HTF machinery turns off.
useHTF_e = useHTFTrend and not timeframe.isdwm
htfTf    = timeframe.isdwm ? "W" : (useAutoHTF ? htfAuto : htfTfManual)
localMA  = trendType == "EMA" ? ta.ema(close, trendLen) : ta.sma(close, trendLen)
[htfMA, htfMAprev, htfATR] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf, [localMA[1], localMA[1 + slopeLen], ta.atr(atrLen)[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
trendMA = useHTF_e ? htfMA : localMA
slopeATRval = useHTF_e ? (htfATR > 0 ? (htfMA - htfMAprev) / htfATR : 0.0) : (atr > 0 ? (localMA - localMA[slopeLen]) / atr : 0.0)
slopeUp = slopeATRval >=  slopeMinATR_e
slopeDn = slopeATRval <= -slopeMinATR_e
slopeFlat = useSlope and not slopeUp and not slopeDn
slopeLongOK  = not useSlope or slopeUp
slopeShortOK = not useSlope or slopeDn

// ── Market-index alignment (same-TF security does not repaint) ─────────────────────────
[mktClose, mktMA] = request.security(marketSym, timeframe.period, [close, ta.ema(close, marketMaLen)])
mktLongOK  = not useMarketFilter or mktClose > mktMA
mktShortOK = not useMarketFilter or mktClose < mktMA

// ── Market regime — DISPLAY ONLY, deliberately not wired into any condition ──────────────
// The frozen switch-policy classifier from the pre-registered switch-vs-parallel test:
// SPY above a RISING 50-day SMA, decided on the PRIOR daily close. Note this is a
// different measure from the market filter above (that one is EMA, no rising test) and is
// pinned to DAILY bars regardless of chart timeframe, because that is how it was tested.
// Indexing [1] / [6] takes the last COMPLETED daily bar, so the label cannot repaint.
// It is NOT referenced by goLong/goShort or any exit — combining the engines was measured
// and LOST on a single symbol (-30.7% MAR vs momentum alone on PRI, 2026-07-30), because
// v4 already contains its own market filter. The switch only pays at PORTFOLIO level.
regimeUp = request.security(marketSym, "D",
     close[1] > ta.sma(close, 50)[1] and ta.sma(close, 50)[1] > ta.sma(close, 50)[6],
     lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)

// ── Swing structure for stops ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
swingLow  = ta.lowest(low,  structLookback)
swingHigh = ta.highest(high, structLookback)

// ── Momentum: Impulse MACD, MACD, RSI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
srcImp = hlc3
impHi = calc_smma(high, lengthMA)
impLo = calc_smma(low,  lengthMA)
mi    = calc_zlema(srcImp, lengthMA)
md    = mi > impHi ? mi - impHi : mi < impLo ? mi - impLo : 0.0
sb    = ta.sma(md, lengthSignal)
impBull = not useImpulse or md > sb
impBear = not useImpulse or md < sb
[macdValue, signalValue, macdHist] = ta.macd(close, fastLength, slowLength, signalLength)
macdBullRaw = macdValue > signalValue
macdBearRaw = macdValue < signalValue
macdBull = not useMACDGate or macdBullRaw
macdBear = not useMACDGate or macdBearRaw
rsiValue = ta.rsi(close, rsiLength)
rsiLongOK  = not useRSIGate or rsiValue > rsiLongLevel_e
rsiShortOK = not useRSIGate or rsiValue < rsiShortLevel_e

// ── Filters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[diPlus, diMinus, adxValue] = ta.dmi(adxLen, adxLen)
adxOK  = not useADX or adxValue >= adxMin_e
inSess = not useSess or not na(time(timeframe.period, sess))
filtersOK = adxOK and inSess
candleBuyOK  = not useCandle or close > open
candleSellOK = not useCandle or close < open
extLongOK  = not useExtLong  or srcExtLong  > extLevel
extShortOK = not useExtShort or srcExtShort > extLevel

// ── Confluence states + triggers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
longState  = slopeLongOK  and macdBull and impBull and rsiLongOK  and filtersOK
shortState = slopeShortOK and macdBear and impBear and rsiShortOK and filtersOK
longTrig   = longState  and not longState[1]
shortTrig  = shortState and not shortState[1]

confirmed = not confirmClose or barstate.isconfirmed
var int lastSigBar = na
cooled = na(lastSigBar) or (bar_index - lastSigBar) >= minBarsBetween

emaFast   = ta.ema(close, pullbackEMA)
pullLong  = usePullback and longState  and ta.crossover(close, emaFast)
pullShort = usePullback and shortState and ta.crossunder(close, emaFast)

stLong  = useStateEntry and longTrig
stShort = useStateEntry and shortTrig
goLong  = allowLongs  and (stLong  or pullLong)  and mktLongOK  and cooled and candleBuyOK  and extLongOK  and inWindow
goShort = allowShorts and (stShort or pullShort) and mktShortOK and cooled and candleSellOK and extShortOK and inWindow

// ── Position bookkeeping ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var int   lastDir   = 0
var float slLong    = na
var float tpLong    = na
var float slShort   = na
var float tpShort   = na
var float riskLong  = na
var float riskShort = na
var float entryPx   = na
var bool  beDone    = false

isLong  = strategy.position_size > 0
isShort = strategy.position_size < 0
exitLongCond  = (exitOnMACD and macdBearRaw) or (exitOnTrend_e and close < trendMA) or (exitOnRSI and ta.crossunder(rsiValue, 50))
exitShortCond = (exitOnMACD and macdBullRaw) or (exitOnTrend_e and close > trendMA) or (exitOnRSI and ta.crossover(rsiValue, 50))

canLong  = goLong  and (allowReentry or lastDir != 1)
canShort = goShort and (allowReentry or lastDir != -1)
doLong  = longWinsOnConflict ? canLong : (canLong  and not canShort)
doShort = longWinsOnConflict ? (canShort and not canLong) : (canShort and not canLong)

buy       = false
sell      = false
exitLong  = false
exitShort = false

if confirmed
    if isLong and exitLongCond and not doShort
        strategy.close("Long", comment="exitL")
        exitLong := true
    if isShort and exitShortCond and not doLong
        strategy.close("Short", comment="exitS")
        exitShort := true
    if doLong
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long)
        buy := true
        lastDir := 1
        lastSigBar := bar_index
        rawRiskL = close - (swingLow - structBufATR * atr)
        rL = (useStructStop and rawRiskL > 0) ? math.max(rawRiskL, atrStopMult * atr * 0.5) : atrStopMult * atr
        riskLong := rL
        slLong := close - rL
        tpLong := close + rrRatio_e * rL
        entryPx := close
        beDone := false
    if doShort
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short)
        sell := true
        lastDir := -1
        lastSigBar := bar_index
        rawRiskS = (swingHigh + structBufATR * atr) - close
        rS = (useStructStop and rawRiskS > 0) ? math.max(rawRiskS, atrStopMult * atr * 0.5) : atrStopMult * atr
        riskShort := rS
        slShort := close + rS
        tpShort := close - rrRatio_e * rS
        entryPx := close
        beDone := false

// Breakeven & stop/target orders (broker emulator: conservative when stop+target share a bar)
if useBreakeven_e and isLong  and not na(entryPx) and high >= entryPx + beTriggerR * riskLong
    beDone := true
if useBreakeven_e and isShort and not na(entryPx) and low  <= entryPx - beTriggerR * riskShort
    beDone := true

stopLnow = (useBreakeven_e and beDone) ? entryPx : slLong
stopSnow = (useBreakeven_e and beDone) ? entryPx : slShort
if exitOnTarget and isLong and not na(slLong)
    if usePartial_e
        strategy.exit("L-TP1", from_entry="Long", qty_percent=partialPct, limit=entryPx + partialR * riskLong, stop=stopLnow)
    strategy.exit("L-Exit", from_entry="Long", limit=tpLong, stop=stopLnow)
if exitOnTarget and isShort and not na(slShort)
    if usePartial_e
        strategy.exit("S-TP1", from_entry="Short", qty_percent=partialPct, limit=entryPx - partialR * riskShort, stop=stopSnow)
    strategy.exit("S-Exit", from_entry="Short", limit=tpShort, stop=stopSnow)

// ── Chart output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
trendCol = slopeFlat ? color.new(color.gray, 0) : (slopeUp ? color.new(color.teal, 0) : slopeDn ? color.new(color.red, 0) : color.new(color.gray, 40))
plot(showTrend ? trendMA : na, "Trend / exit line", color=trendCol, linewidth=2)
plot(usePullback ? emaFast : na, "Fast EMA", color=color.new(color.blue, 55))

// Live stop & target lines while a trade is open — you can SEE the plan on the chart.
plot(showRiskLines and isLong  ? stopLnow : showRiskLines and isShort ? stopSnow : na, "Stop (live)",   color=color.new(color.red, 20),   style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plot(showRiskLines and isLong  ? tpLong   : showRiskLines and isShort ? tpShort  : na, "Target (live)", color=color.new(color.green, 20), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)

if showSignals and allowLongs and buy
    label.new(bar_index, na, buyTag,  yloc=yloc.belowbar, style=label.style_label_up,   color=buyMarkerCol,  textcolor=color.white, size=sizeOpt)
if showSignals and allowShorts and sell
    label.new(bar_index, na, sellTag, yloc=yloc.abovebar, style=label.style_label_down, color=sellMarkerCol, textcolor=color.white, size=sizeOpt)

longSold     = strategy.position_size[1] > 0 and strategy.position_size < strategy.position_size[1]
shortCovered = strategy.position_size[1] < 0 and strategy.position_size > strategy.position_size[1]
plotshape(showSignals and showExits and longSold,     "Sell (exit long)",   shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, sellMarkerCol, text="SELL",  textcolor=color.white,   size=size.normal)
plotshape(showSignals and showExits and shortCovered, "Cover (exit short)", shape.xcross,    location.belowbar, exitMarkerCol, text="COVER", textcolor=exitMarkerCol, size=size.small)

// ── Alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(buy,          "Buy",              "[iAPE_v4] BUY {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(sell,         "Sell (short)",     "[iAPE_v4] SELL (short) {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(longSold,     "Sell (exit long)", "[iAPE_v4] SELL / EXIT LONG {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(shortCovered, "Cover short",      "[iAPE_v4] COVER SHORT {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(buy or sell or longSold or shortCovered, "Any signal", "[iAPE_v4] signal {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")

// ── Connector outputs (hidden) — other scripts can wire these in ─────────────────────────
plot(buy       ? 1 : 0, "→ Buy signal",         color=color.new(color.green, 100), display=display.none)
plot(sell      ? 1 : 0, "→ Sell signal",        color=color.new(color.red,   100), display=display.none)
plot(longSold  ? 1 : 0, "→ Exit long",          color=color.new(color.orange,100), display=display.none)
plot(shortCovered ? 1 : 0, "→ Cover short",     color=color.new(color.orange,100), display=display.none)
plot(strategy.position_size > 0 ? 1 : 0, "→ In long position",  color=color.new(color.gray, 100), display=display.none)
plot(strategy.position_size < 0 ? 1 : 0, "→ In short position", color=color.new(color.gray, 100), display=display.none)

// ── Plain-English dashboard (bottom of the chart window) ─────────────────────────────────
var table dash = table.new(position.bottom_center, 2, 11, frame_width=1,
     frame_color=color.new(color.gray, 40), border_width=1, border_color=color.new(color.gray, 80))

f_row(int r, string k, string v, color vcol) =>
    table.cell(dash, 0, r, k, text_color=color.new(color.white, 15), text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 20), text_size=dashSize)
    table.cell(dash, 1, r, v, text_color=vcol, text_halign=text.align_left,  bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 35), text_size=dashSize)

if barstate.islast and showDash
    grey  = color.new(color.white, 35)
    green = color.new(#26a69a, 0)
    red   = color.new(#ef5350, 0)

    string modeTag = isStrict ? "STRICT (unvalidated)" : isComfort ? "COMFORT (win% dial)" : "v2.2 validated"
    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "iAPE · " + modeTag, text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.new(isStrict ? color.orange : isComfort ? color.blue : color.teal, 15), text_size=dashSize)
    // timeframe.period is "1D"/"1W" on daily+ charts, so the old unconditional "min"
    // suffix rendered "1Dmin chart" once the flagship moved to daily.
    string tfLabel = timeframe.isdwm ? timeframe.period + " chart" : timeframe.period + "min chart"
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, syminfo.ticker + "  ·  " + tfLabel, text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.new(isStrict ? color.orange : isComfort ? color.blue : color.teal, 15), text_size=dashSize)

    string posTxt = "FLAT — waiting for a setup"
    color  posCol = grey
    if isLong
        posTxt := "LONG " + str.tostring(math.abs(strategy.position_size), "#.##") + " shares @ " + str.tostring(strategy.position_avg_price, format.mintick)
        posCol := green
    if isShort
        posTxt := "SHORT " + str.tostring(math.abs(strategy.position_size), "#.##") + " shares @ " + str.tostring(strategy.position_avg_price, format.mintick)
        posCol := red
    f_row(1, "Right now", posTxt, posCol)

    string riskTxt = "—"
    if isLong
        riskTxt := "stop " + str.tostring(stopLnow, format.mintick) + (beDone ? " (moved to breakeven)" : "") + "  →  target " + str.tostring(tpLong, format.mintick)
    if isShort
        riskTxt := "stop " + str.tostring(stopSnow, format.mintick) + (beDone ? " (moved to breakeven)" : "") + "  →  target " + str.tostring(tpShort, format.mintick)
    f_row(2, "The plan", riskTxt, grey)

    openPL = strategy.openprofit
    f_row(3, "Open trade P&L", (isLong or isShort) ? (openPL >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(openPL, "#,###.##") + " USD" : "—",
         openPL > 0 ? green : openPL < 0 ? red : grey)

    tot  = strategy.closedtrades
    wr   = tot > 0 ? 100.0 * strategy.wintrades / tot : na
    f_row(4, "Trades on this chart", str.tostring(tot) + (tot > 0 ? "  (won " + str.tostring(wr, "#.#") + "% of them)" : ""), grey)

    gp = strategy.grossprofit
    gl = strategy.grossloss
    pf = gl > 0 ? gp / gl : na
    string pfTxt = na(pf) ? "—" : "made $" + str.tostring(pf, "#.##") + " for every $1 lost"
    f_row(5, "Profit factor", pfTxt, na(pf) ? grey : pf >= 1.1 ? green : pf >= 0.95 ? grey : red)

    np = strategy.netprofit
    f_row(6, "Net result", (np >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(np, "#,###") + " USD  (" + (np >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(100 * np / strategy.initial_capital, "#.##") + "% of starting capital)",
         np > 0 ? green : np < 0 ? red : grey)

    // live losing streak vs the Monte Carlo "normal weather" threshold (12)
    int streak = 0
    if tot > 0
        for i = 0 to tot - 1
            streak := strategy.closedtrades.profit(i) <= 0 ? streak + 1 : 0
    string stTxt = tot == 0 ? "—" :
         str.tostring(streak) + " in a row  (up to 12 is NORMAL for a working system — Monte Carlo, 10k runs)"
    f_row(7, "Losing streak", stTxt, streak > 12 ? red : streak >= 8 ? color.new(color.orange, 0) : grey)

    // timeframe validation status — which chart is this engine PROVEN on?
    string tfStat = timeframe.isdwm ? "DAILY — VALIDATED on a decade (PF 2.2-2.7 across 23 symbols; overnight gaps can slip stops)" :
         timeframe.period == "5" ? "5-min — VALIDATED (2y, PF 1.30, both halves)" :
         timeframe.period == "1" ? "1-min — REJECTED (PF 0.82, 0/5 symbols; do not trade this)" :
         timeframe.period == "60" ? "1-hour — FAILED validation (all gains were year-one)" :
         "UNVALIDATED at this timeframe — signals shown, trust not earned"
    color tfCol = timeframe.isdwm or timeframe.period == "5" ? green :
         timeframe.period == "1" or timeframe.period == "60" ? red : color.new(color.orange, 0)
    f_row(8, "This timeframe", tfStat, tfCol)

    string verdict = tot < 30 ? "Too few trades here to judge — load more history" :
         na(pf) ? "No losing trades yet — sample too small to trust" :
         pf >= 1.15 ? "Profitable on this chart — verify on other symbols & dates before trusting it" :
         pf >= 0.95 ? "About breakeven after costs on this chart" :
         "Losing money on this chart — do not trade these settings live"
    f_row(9, "Plain verdict", verdict, tot < 30 ? grey : na(pf) ? grey : pf >= 1.15 ? green : pf >= 0.95 ? grey : red)

    // Regime read-out. Colour is deliberately NEUTRAL in both states — this is weather,
    // not an instruction, and green/red here would read as "trade / don't trade".
    if showRegime
        string regTxt = regimeUp ?
             "MOMENTUM weather — SPY above a rising 50-day (label only; entries unchanged)" :
             "MEAN-REVERSION weather — SPY not in an uptrend (label only; entries unchanged)"
        f_row(10, "Market regime", regTxt, grey)
